# Nested Frechet (W2) ANOVA of per-electrode ISI distributions — mid DIV [9, 10, 11], vehicle control

Per-electrode distribution: EMPIRICAL quantile function of log10(ISI ms) (sensitivity: no mixture model); electrodes need >= 30 ISIs; thinned to >= 150 um; wells kept with >= 10 thinned electrodes: 32 wells in 7 runs, N = 1281 electrodes (m per well 10-104). Quantile grid K = 200.

## Frechet ANOVA table (SS in (log10 ISI)^2 units, L2 on quantile functions)

| source            |       SS |   df |      MS |    F_stat |   perm_p |
|:------------------|---------:|-----:|--------:|----------:|---------:|
| Run               |  16.4454 |    6 | 2.7409  |   4.40665 |   0.0008 |
| Well(Run)         |  15.5498 |   25 | 0.62199 |   2.9265  |   0.0002 |
| Electrode (resid) | 265.46   | 1249 | 0.21254 | nan       | nan      |

F_stat is the usual ratio MS_run/MS_well(run) and MS_well(run)/MS_e; its null distribution is NOT F, p-values are from 5000 permutations.

